# gymact-bridge-pack: admitted facts for the ggen<->GymAct bridge.
#
# NOT a custom ontology. Every class/property used here is either (a) from
# `ontology/profile.ttl`/`ontology/profile.shacl.ttl` -- real, relative
# SYMLINKS to `src/gymact/ontology/profile.{ttl,shacl.ttl}` in this SAME
# repo (not a copy, not vendored from elsewhere -- this pack was moved
# here from a sibling `ggen` repo, where those two files started as a
# drift-checked external copy; now that pack and profile share one repo,
# the symlink makes drift structurally impossible instead of merely
# detectable) -- or (b) a public term reused directly (dct:, sosa:),
# following this repo's own prefix-reuse convention
# (ggen-combinatorial-maximalism-pack/ontology.ttl, in the sibling `ggen`
# repo, is the origin of that convention).
#
# HISTORY: an earlier version of this pack invented its own `gab:Operation`
# rdfs:Class, `gab:consequenceClass` property, and locally-scoped
# `gab:Read`/`gab:Do` SKOS individuals -- before the real `gymact` repo
# existed. Once `~/gymact` shipped for real (v26.8.7), reading it directly
# showed that vocabulary was pure invention: the real capability class is
# `sosa:Procedure` (not `Operation`), and the real consequence-class IRIs
# are `urn:gymact:consequence:read`/`urn:gymact:consequence:do` (not a
# project-local `gab:` namespace). Real GymAct's own admission code
# (`src/gymact/semantic.py`'s `ProfileAuthority._custom_tbox_terms()`)
# mechanically REJECTS exactly the kind of custom-TBox individual the old
# version of this file declared -- proven live by
# `~/gymact/tests/test_semantic_capability.py::
# test_extension_cannot_smuggle_custom_gymact_tbox`. This file is the
# corrected version: it declares zero new rdfs:Class/owl:*Property terms,
# only `sosa:Procedure` INSTANCES (data, not vocabulary) satisfying the
# real `urn:gymact:shape:capability` SHACL shape.
#
# The 4 capabilities below are a deliberately small subset of the real 8
# values GymAct's own `gymact.models.Operation` StrEnum defines (discover,
# materialize, observe, act, verify, checkpoint, restore, teardown) --
# proof-of-mechanism scope, not the full taxonomy. `dct:title` carries the
# exact enum string so a real gymact consumer could recognize these as its
# own operation names; `dct:type` is set per the real Operation semantics:
# `act` is GymAct's one world-changing operation (-> consequence:do), the
# other three are observation-only (-> consequence:read).

@prefix dct:  <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .
@prefix sosa: <http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/> .

<urn:gymact:bridge:capability:discover>
    a sosa:Procedure ;
    dct:title "discover" ;
    dct:type <urn:gymact:consequence:read> .

<urn:gymact:bridge:capability:observe>
    a sosa:Procedure ;
    dct:title "observe" ;
    dct:type <urn:gymact:consequence:read> .

<urn:gymact:bridge:capability:act>
    a sosa:Procedure ;
    dct:title "act" ;
    dct:type <urn:gymact:consequence:do> .

<urn:gymact:bridge:capability:verify>
    a sosa:Procedure ;
    dct:title "verify" ;
    dct:type <urn:gymact:consequence:read> .
